{
  "scope": "CPU-only complete-DD workspace reuse. Production change is confined to the existing opt-in windowed helper; no arithmetic, key, scale, modulus, prime, tree or precision changes.",
  "implementation_commit": "1e87ae5",
  "workspace": "Allocate tensor, lifted-mask, switched-ciphertext and exception vectors once at min(window,product_count). Reuse them across all complete-product windows and pass only the active prefix to the gadget kernel. Buffers remain local to one invocation and are destroyed on return. Peak capacity remains bounded by the requested window.",
  "overwrites": "Tensor multiplication clears/reconstructs every component, lifting overwrites each input polynomial, and the gadget batch clears every active switched output including zero inputs. A zero-valued partial tail after a nonzero window is checked explicitly at full ring size.",
  "control": "dd_scratch_candidate.hpp freezes the previous production function from0aa6604, changing only its name and namespace. Its normalized body was checked byte-for-byte against git show. Benchmark modes use the same typed borrowed products, prepared key and ciphertext operands.",
  "unit_coverage": "Exact final ciphertext equality at all five LL14 data levels, N16/512/16384, mixed zero/midpoint/noncanonical inputs, partial windows3/8/16, and nine-product zero tails. Null-pointer and zero-window guards remain effective. Scalar x86-64/no-AVX2 build and primary20/40 forest/odd-carry checks pass.",
